%T A400690 0,10,10,12,24,30,12,8,2,8,42,2,8,20,24,0,0,30,8,20,0,0,36,0,18,0,8,
%U A400690 40,30,0,12,6,0,2,26,12,0,0,8,0,18,0,12,2,2,44,2,0
%N A400690 Span of the n-th maximal cluster of primes with consecutive gaps at most 8.
%C A400690 Whether a later cluster has span >111 remains unresolved here. The Hardy-Littlewood prime-tuples conjecture predicts later clusters with span at least 188, based on an admissible pattern with gaps at most 8. Later spans are even, so equality with the initial span is impossible.
%C A400690 For jump limits 2, 4 and 6, the initial spans 5, 21 and 87 are provably unique maxima since every later cluster has span at most 2, 16 and 78, respectively.
%C A400690 For limit 10, the initial span 111 is exceeded by the cluster 331 to 467, with span 136.
%H A400690 Jwalin Bhatt, <a href="/A400690/b400690.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A400690 The first cluster is 2,...,113 and has span 113-2=111, so a(1)=111. The next two clusters are {127,131,137,139} and {149,151,157,163,167,173,179,181}, giving a(2)=12 and a(3)=32. The fifth cluster is {211}, so a(5)=0.
%o A400690 (Python)
%o A400690 from sympy import nextprime
%o A400690 from itertools import islice
%o A400690 def gen_A400690():
%o A400690     start = p = 2
%o A400690     while True:
%o A400690         q = int(nextprime(p))
%o A400690         if q - p > 8:
%o A400690             yield p - start
%o A400690             start = q
%o A400690         p = q
%o A400690 print(list(islice(gen_A400690(), 75)))
